      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JUGIONG (2) resumes as the one to beat, with his best form reading well for this on metro tracks. He was only beaten two lengths at Sandown-Lakeside before the break and is already a winner at this track and distance, with two wins from three starts at 1000m adding weight to the case. Races best early in the prep. ZEMGRINDA (3) was unwanted and slow away first-up at Hamilton but was not beaten far in BM70 grade, and his broader record on good tracks and around this trip makes him the logical danger with his good second-up record. MARINE GIRL (9) brings the most consistent recent profile, having been beaten a length and a half at both Bathurst and Cootamundra, while her record with Coriah Keatings keeps her firmly in the minor-money mix. TROOPER (4) resumes off an easy Canberra trial and has winning form at the distance, though he has to rebound from a plain favourite defeat before the break. No shock to see him take this out.",
